course: dictionary
lesson: 12023
title: What is chloride?
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A chloride is a chemical made when chlorine joins with another element. The name gives a clue: chlor- comes from chlorine, and -ide shows that two things have joined together. «Sodium chloride» is sodium joined to chlorine.
explain: Sodium chloride is the scientific name for table salt. When you sprinkle salt on your chips, you are adding sodium chloride. «Calcium chloride» and «potassium chloride» are other chlorides, each with a different element joined to the chlorine.
explain: Chloride can also mean the chloride ion, which is a chlorine atom with one extra electron. You will not find these on their own. They are dissolved in sea water and in our bodies. Ask yourself whether the word means a whole chemical or a single ion. The sentence around it will tell you.
fact: A chloride is a compound: chlorine joined with another element.
fact: The best known chloride is sodium chloride, which is common table salt.
fact: The chloride ion is a chlorine atom with an extra electron.
fact: Chloride ions are dissolved in sea water and in our bodies.
fact: Other chlorides include «calcium chloride» and «potassium chloride».
exercise: «Mum added a pinch of sodium chloride to the soup.» What is sodium chloride? | *Table salt | A type of sand | A gas you breathe | A red liquid
exercise: «Sea water contains chloride ions dissolved in it.» Where are chloride ions found? | Floating in the air we breathe | *In sea water and in our bodies | Growing in the bark of trees | Inside the moon
exercise: «The label on the bottle said potassium chloride.» What does the word chloride tell you? | *That chlorine is joined to another element | That the bottle is empty | That the bottle is made of wood | That the bottle holds a fruit
test: What is «calcium chloride» made of? | Calcium joined to oxygen | *Calcium joined to chlorine | Helium joined to hydrogen | Iron joined to chlorine
test: What is the best known chloride, the one in table salt? | Potassium chloride | Calcium chloride | Chloride ion | *Sodium chloride
exam: A chloride ion is best described as | *A chlorine atom with an extra electron | A thin metal wire | A chemical that makes you hungry | A gas that floats in the air
